  "conclusion": "The six completion substages explain 99.95% of the full-run completion latency. Pool acquisition is negligible, while transaction begin, advisory lock, identity read, delete, and commit are serialized per message. The next bounded experiment is a completion committer that batches only already verified published intents, preserves sorted advisory-lock acquisition, validates every complete identity before deletion, reduces rather than increases PostgreSQL transaction count, and reconciles unknown commit outcomes per intent.",
